course: dictionary
lesson: 6069
title: Merrily and the mood of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Merrily is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. In «jumping merrily along hand in hand», the word merrily tells you how the children jumped: in a happy, cheerful way. Find the action word first, then ask how it was done.
explain: Merrily can also mean carelessly, without thinking about trouble. «He merrily ignored the warning» means he ignored it without caring what might go wrong. The clue is in the sentence: a warning is something you should pay attention to, so ignoring it so cheerfully is careless.
explain: Songs and carols use merrily to make the mood bright. «Row, row, row your boat, gently down the stream, merrily, merrily, merrily, merrily, life is but a dream.» To check your meaning, swap in "happily" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Merrily is an adverb, a word that tells how something is done.
fact: «Merrily» means in a happy, cheerful, jolly way.
fact: «Merrily» can also mean carelessly, without thinking about trouble.
fact: «Ding dong merrily on high» is a Christmas carol, and the word tells the reader that things are cheerful.
fact: A good check is to swap in "happily" or "cheerfully" and see if the sentence still works.
exercise: In the procession, the royal children were «jumping merrily along hand in hand». How were they moving? | *In a happy, cheerful way | Quietly, in silence | Slowly and sadly | Angrily, stamping their feet
exercise: «He merrily ignored the warning.» What does merrily mean here? | *Carelessly, without thinking about trouble | Very carefully and slowly | Sadly, with tears in his eyes | Loudly and angrily
exercise: Find and copy the adverb in this sentence: «The bells rang merrily across the village.» | bells | *merrily | village | rang
test: «The children danced merrily around the tree.» Which word tells how they danced? | tree | *merrily | danced | around
test: In the song «gently down the stream, merrily, merrily», what mood does merrily suggest? | Sadness and tiredness | Anger and shouting | *Happiness and cheerfulness | Fear of the water
exam: Which meaning fits merrily best in «He merrily ignored the warning», and why? | Sadly, because he was upset | *Carelessly, because he did not think about the trouble the warning described | Loudly, because he was shouting | Very quickly, because he was in a rush
